---
description: Breadcrumbs for hierarchy; action forms use Cancel then Save, right-aligned
globs: client/app/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Page navigation: Breadcrumbs / Cancel / Save

Classify each App Router page as a **view** or **action** page.

## Breadcrumbs (all app pages)

- Place `Breadcrumbs` from `@/components/ui/Breadcrumbs` at the top of the page (above the title)
- Trail must include every ancestor so users can return to previous pages (e.g. Home / Surveys / Create)
- Last crumb is the current page (no link); earlier crumbs are links
- Home is always the first crumb (`href: '/'`) for nested routes
- Do not rely on browser back; do not use a separate "Return to …" control when breadcrumbs cover the parent path

```tsx
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/ui/Breadcrumbs';

<Breadcrumbs
  items={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Surveys', href: '/surveys' },
    { label: 'Create' },
  ]}
/>
```

## View pages

Read-only or browse surfaces (lists, detail/results, dashboards).

- Breadcrumbs only for upward navigation
- Do not put Save/Cancel on view pages

## Action pages

Create, edit, submit, or other mutating forms (`/new`, `/edit`, answer/submit flows).

- Breadcrumbs in the header (same as view pages)
- Form footer must include **Cancel** then **Save** (or Create / Submit), in that order
- **Cancel** is first (leftmost of the group, bordered secondary); **Save** is last (rightmost, primary accent)
- Align the whole action group to the **right** (`flex flex-wrap justify-end`); see `.cursor/rules/form-action-buttons.mdc`
- **Cancel** navigates to the parent list/detail (same as the breadcrumb parent) and does not submit
- For embedded create/edit forms on list pages, Cancel clears the form fields instead of navigating away

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-wrap justify-end gap-3">
  <Link
    href="/surveys"
    className="rounded-md border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-[var(--accent-soft)]"
  >
    Cancel
  </Link>
  <button type="submit" disabled={saving} className="rounded-md bg-[var(--accent)] px-4 py-2 font-medium text-white ...">
    {saving ? 'Saving…' : 'Save'}
  </button>
</div>
```

## Modals

- Footer actions also use **Cancel** then primary confirm/save, right-aligned

## Do not

- Put Save before Cancel
- Left-align form/page/modal action buttons (keep the group `justify-end`)
- Omit Cancel on action forms
- Omit breadcrumbs on nested app pages
- Use `router.back()` as the only way to leave an action page
